From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: count equal-acquires whose value already went by (idea: CheezerWheezer, CheezyEmu 243c19bdf2), EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT=1, off by default (count only)

Switch: EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT=1 (exact 1, read once at the first unmet drained poll).
Unset: no line.

What: a channel suspended on an "equal" semaphore acquire waits for one exact value. If the
release it waits for happened and later releases moved the word on before the channel looked
(the waiter latch only catches releases made while the channel waits), that value never comes
again and the channel waits for good: the game hangs. CheezyEmu's commit: a tester's game hung for
good during a song in Ocarina ("waits on semaphore ... (op 1, 0x19f1c, now 0x19f72)"). Upstream
then lets the channel go on after 250 ms. This patch only counts: in CanResumeAcquire's drained
path, after the word was read and did not match, an equal-acquire that has waited 250 ms or more
with the word 1 to 1 << 20 past its value gets one line (once per wait): channel, ms waited,
address, value, word, how far past, and a running count. First 64 lines, then every 64th. The
channel keeps waiting as before. Nothing else changes.

Why count first: it shows whether the recent hard freezes include this kind of hang before we let
a channel skip a wait (on: a frame may run out of order). The existing 2 s line ("Channel n waits
on semaphore ... (op 1, value, now word)") already shows such waits when they last 2 s; this line
names them, catches them at 250 ms and counts them over a session.

Where: video_core/engines/puller.h (PendingAcquire::passed_noted, WaitsForEqual), puller.cpp
(NotePassedAcquire in the anonymous namespace, one call in CanResumeAcquire after the drained
read). With EDEN_NX2_SEM_FAST or EDEN_UP_L949_ACQUIRE the drained path is taken less often (after
2 s, or at the 1 ms valve), so the line can come later than 250 ms there.

Differences from upstream: no "go on" (that is a later step), so also no extra DrainBack and word
read in the poll without a drain (upstream adds one every 50 ms past 250 ms); our puller has no
PollWithoutDrain. Switch name, once-per-wait flag and count ours.

Origin and credit: CheezerWheezer, CheezyEmu (github.com/CheezerWheezer/CheezyEmu) commit
243c19bdf2 "GPU: an equal-acquire whose value went by no longer hangs the game", 12 Nov 2026,
GPL-3.0 (its switch EDEN_NX2_PASSED_ACQUIRE is on by default there). The 250 ms and 1 << 20 bounds
are upstream's.

Off: one function call with a cached bool test per unmet drained poll (at most every 2 ms per
waiting channel with the split GPU thread). No shader translation change, no shader-store stamp
change.

Test: count only, in the next long sessions (and any session that froze). Look at: the
"EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT" lines, and whether one comes right before a freeze. Pass to make
the "go on" version: the line shows at least once; then the same spot with going on, no hang, no
visible fault.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp
index f081fcae5e..91a94717db 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "common/assert.h"
 #include "common/live_switch.h"
 #include "common/logging.h"
+#include "common/pe_switch.h"
 #include "common/settings.h"
 #include "core/core.h"
 #include "video_core/nx2_profile.h"
@@ -409,6 +410,38 @@ bool MetAfterPendingRelease(const DmaPusher& dma_pusher, GPUVAddr address, const
     return true;
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT=1 (0744, count only; the idea is CheezerWheezer's, CheezyEmu
+// 243c19bdf2): an equal-acquire whose value the semaphore has already gone past. The release it
+// waits for happened, and later ones moved the word on, before this channel looked (the waiter
+// latch only catches releases made while it waits), so nothing will write that value again and
+// the channel waits for good (CheezyEmu: a tester's game hung for good during a song, the word at
+// 0x19f72 while 0x19f1c was waited for). Counted once per wait, after 250 ms with the word at
+// most 1 << 20 past the value (a small ring of values that comes round again is left alone).
+// Upstream then lets the channel go on; this build only counts and keeps waiting.
+void NotePassedAcquire(DmaPusher& dma_pusher, Puller::PendingAcquire& acquire, u32 current) {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT");
+    if (!enabled || acquire.passed_noted || !acquire.WaitsForEqual()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    const auto waited = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - acquire.since;
+    const u32 ahead = current - acquire.value;
+    if (waited < std::chrono::milliseconds{250} || ahead == 0 || ahead > (1U << 20)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    acquire.passed_noted = true;
+    static std::atomic<u64> passed{};
+    const u64 count = passed.fetch_add(1) + 1;
+    if (count <= 64 || count % 64 == 0) {
+        LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU,
+                    "EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT: channel {} has waited {} ms for semaphore "
+                    "{:#x} to equal {:#x}, already passed (now {:#x}, {:#x} ahead); keeps waiting "
+                    "({} such waits so far)",
+                    dma_pusher.channel_state.bind_id,
+                    std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(waited).count(),
+                    acquire.address, acquire.value, current, ahead, count);
+    }
+}
+
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 bool Puller::PendingAcquire::Matches(u32 current) const {
@@ -428,6 +461,10 @@ bool Puller::PendingAcquire::WaitsToReach() const {
     return static_cast<GpuSemaphoreOperation>(operation) == GpuSemaphoreOperation::AcquireGequal;
 }
 
+bool Puller::PendingAcquire::WaitsForEqual() const {
+    return static_cast<GpuSemaphoreOperation>(operation) == GpuSemaphoreOperation::AcquireEqual;
+}
+
 bool Puller::CanResumeAcquire(DmaPusher& dma_pusher) {
     if (!pending_acquire) {
         return true;
@@ -519,6 +556,7 @@ bool Puller::CanResumeAcquire(DmaPusher& dma_pusher) {
     if (pending_acquire->Matches(current)) {
         return true;
     }
+    NotePassedAcquire(dma_pusher, *pending_acquire, current); // 0744, count only
     // With delayed fence operations (Balanced or Accurate fences, accurate GPU), a release
     // queued after the acquire released the fences waits in the caches for the next fence. With
     // every channel waiting none comes: release them again now and then while waiting.
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/puller.h b/src/video_core/engines/puller.h
index b232182b75..b8cfd7d194 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/puller.h
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/puller.h
@@ -85,10 +85,14 @@ public:
         /// EDEN_UP_L949_ACQUIRE, EDEN_UP_L949_DRAIN_VALVE: when an unmet poll last drained (the
         /// 1 ms valve); unset means since the acquire began.
         std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point last_drain{};
+        /// EDEN_UP_PASSED_ACQUIRE_COUNT (0744): this wait was already counted as passed by.
+        bool passed_noted{};
 
         [[nodiscard]] bool Matches(u32 current) const;
         /// Whether it waits for the word to reach `value` (greater or equal).
         [[nodiscard]] bool WaitsToReach() const;
+        /// Whether it waits for the word to equal `value` exactly (0744).
+        [[nodiscard]] bool WaitsForEqual() const;
     };
 
     [[nodiscard]] bool HasPendingAcquire() const {
